Package: tuxdisplay
Version: 0.3.0
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TuxDisplay contributors <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, xvfb, x11vnc, novnc, websockify, openbox, tint2, xterm, x11-utils, x11-xserver-utils, xauth, iproute2, network-manager, avahi-daemon, polkitd, pkexec, dnsmasq-base, libimobiledevice-utils, usbmuxd, ipheth-utils
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, firefox | chromium | chromium-browser
Homepage: https://github.com/tpluharik/tuxdisplay
Description: use an iPad browser as a USB or network secondary monitor
 TuxDisplay creates a real extended monitor in GNOME Wayland and exposes it
 through a touch-capable browser client. It supports LAN, iPad USB tethering,
 and optional USB gadget Ethernet. Other desktops use an X11 workspace fallback.
